+Prints totals per category. Omit `--month` to see all time. Narrow to one
+category with `--category`.
 
 ```
-python -m tally.cli list --month 2024-03
-python -m tally.cli export --out march.csv
+tally report --month 2024-03
+tally report --month 2024-03 --category food
+```
+
+### list — individual expenses
+
 ```
+tally list [--month YYYY-MM] [--category NAME]
+```
+
+Shows each expense as a line rather than rolled-up totals. Accepts the same
+filters as `report`.
+
+### budget — spending vs monthly limits
+
+```
+tally budget --month YYYY-MM
+```
+
+Compares what you spent in each category against the monthly budgets configured
+in `tally/config.py`. Categories over 80 % of their limit are flagged.
+
+```
+tally budget --month 2024-03
+```
+
+### stats — overall summary
 
-## How amounts are stored
+```
+tally stats
+```
+
+Prints total count, sum, average, and the date range covered by the store.
+
+### export — write CSV
+
+```
+tally export [--out FILE]
+```
+
+Writes all expenses as CSV. Without `--out`, output goes to stdout.
+
+```
+tally export --out march.csv
+```
+
+## A typical session
+
+```
+$ tally add 12.50 food --note "lunch"
+added #1: 12.50 USD  food  2026-07-05
+
+$ tally add 39 food --currency EUR
+added #2: 42.12 USD  food  2026-07-05
+
+$ tally report --month 2026-07
+food          54.62 USD
+
+$ tally budget --month 2026-07
+food              54.62 /    600.00 USD  ok
+transport          0.00 /    200.00 USD  ok
+rent               0.00 /   1500.00 USD  ok
+entertainment      0.00 /    150.00 USD  ok
+other              0.00 /    300.00 USD  ok
+```
+
+## Running the tests
+
+```
+python -m pytest
+```
 
-Whenever you add an expense, tally converts the amount into US dollars using the
-conversion table in `tally/rates.py` and stores that dollar figure. The original
-amount and currency you typed are kept alongside it for reference, but every total
-you ever see is computed in US dollars. This keeps reports consistent even when a
-month mixes several currencies.
+The suite must stay green with zero failures and zero warnings.
 
-## A note on scope
+## Scope
 
-This is a personal tool, not an accounting package. It does not do tax categories,
-receipts, shared budgets, or anything clever with recurring expenses. If you need
-those, you have outgrown tally. If you just want to know whether you spent too much
-on takeout last month, you are in the right place.
